BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (  In the beginning, two rivers flowed through a barren land-the River of Dawn and the River of D) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (    usk. Each possessed water, but neither could nurture the valley alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (  The River of Dawn spoke first: "I shall send my waters forward, trusting they will return enri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (    ched." And so it released its flow into the channels between them. As the waters traveled, t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (    hey multiplied threefold, transformed by the valley's ancient magic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  The River of Dusk received this abundance and faced a choice. A voice whispered, "Keep all for) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (     yourself-you have received much." But Dusk remembered that dawn comes again, that rivers fl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (    ow in cycles, not lines.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  "What flows to me came from trust," Dusk said. "I shall return enough that both of us flourish) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    ." And so Dusk sent back waters generously, keeping only what sustained its own course.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  Season after season, the rivers continued their exchange. Each learned the rhythm of giving an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    d receiving. When Dawn gave freely, Dusk returned fairly. The valley between them bloomed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (  The elders say: prosperity flows not to those who hoard, but to those who understand that what) Tj ET
