BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  # The Spring of Threefold Return) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (  In ancient times, when the world was young, there existed a sacred spring at the boundary betw) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    een two villages. The goddess of abundance had blessed it with a wondrous property: any gift) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (     poured into its waters would triple before reaching the other side.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (  The first villagers approached with caution. A farmer named Elena stood at the spring's edge, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    clutching five copper coins. Fear whispered: "Keep what is yours." But trust urged her forwa) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (    rd. She released three coins into the crystalline water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  As the coins sank, they shimmered and multiplied, becoming nine by the time they reached Marcu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    s on the opposite shore. He gazed at the unexpected bounty, understanding the spring's magic) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (    -and Elena's faith in him.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  The goddess watched, knowing this moment would define their future. Would Marcus honor the gif) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (    t, or betray the trust?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (  Marcus carefully counted four coins and released them back across the spring. They did not mul) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    tiply in return, yet both villagers stood richer than before-not just in copper, but in some) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    thing more precious.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (  From that day forward, the spring taught all who approached: generosity multiplies abundance, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    but only trust and reciprocity sustain it. Those who hoarded broke the sacred cycle. Those w) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    ho gave and returned fairly prospered together, generation after generation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (Reasoning:) Tj ET
