BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (  # The Tale of the Twin Rivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  In the time before time, two rivers flowed through a barren valley-the River of Giving and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (     River of Return. Each was controlled by a guardian spirit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  The Guardian of Giving held precious water but feared releasing it would leave them dry. For a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    ges, both rivers remained still, and the valley stayed desolate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  One day, the Guardian of Giving made a bold choice. "I shall release my waters, trusting they ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    will return." The moment the water flowed into the valley, it touched the Sacred Stones, mul) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (    tiplying threefold. The valley burst into bloom.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (  The Guardian of Return, witnessing this abundance, faced a choice. They could hoard all the mu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    ltiplied bounty or honor the trust given. Remembering that without the initial gift there wo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (    uld be nothing, they sent back a generous portion-more than what was originally given.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  The waters flowed in harmony thereafter. Each cycle, the Guardian of Giving would release thei) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (    r waters, the Sacred Stones would multiply them, and the Guardian of Return would ensure fai) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (    r winds brought abundance home.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (  The valley became paradise, teaching all who witnessed: *Trust multiplies what we share, but o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (    nly reciprocity sustains the cycle.*) Tj ET
