BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      # The Myth of the River's Gift) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      In ancient times, there lived a river spirit named Aquila who possessed five silver fish e) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        ach dawn. Along the riverbank dwelt eight villages, and each day Aquila would visit one ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        village, offering her bounty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      When Aquila gave her fish to a villager, the river's magic transformed them-each fish beca) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (        me three as it touched mortal hands. The villager could then choose: keep all the multip) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        lied catch, or return some to Aquila's sacred pool.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      The first villages were fearful and greedy. They clutched every fish tightly, returning no) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        thing. Aquila still visited, still offered her five fish, but her spirit grew dim.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      Then came a village that understood the river's rhythm. When they received fifteen fish fr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        om Aquila's gift of five, they returned seven to the sacred pool. Aquila's spirit bright) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (        ened, and when she visited again, her generosity flowed stronger.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      The wise villages learned: trust begets trust, and generosity returns like water to the se) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        a. When both spirit and mortal honored the cycle-one risking their gift, the other shari) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (        ng the multiplication-the river never ran dry, and abundance sustained all.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      Thus, the ancients taught: what flows forth with trust returns threefold, but only when bo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (        th currents honor the sacred exchange.) Tj ET
BT /F2 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    reasoning:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      I need to write a 200-word myth that reflects how the trust game should be played. Since t) Tj ET
