BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      # The Tale of the Two Springs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      In the ancient highlands, there lived two farmers, Kael and Mira, each tending barren plot) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        s separated by a sacred grove. One day, Kael discovered a hidden spring on his land. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (         water was blessed with a peculiar magic: when poured upon another's soil, it would trip) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        le in volume.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      Kael faced a choice. He could hoard the water for himself, or trust it to Mira's hands. Af) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        ter much contemplation, he carried his precious bucket across the grove.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      "I offer you this water," he said. "Though it multiplies on your land, I trust you will re) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (        turn what sustains us both.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      Mira watched the single bucket become three upon her soil. Her heart swelled with gratitud) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        e. She understood the gift was not just water, but faith itself. She returned two bucket) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (        s to Kael, keeping one for her needs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      With what flowed back, Kael's fields flourished. Seeing this, he sent more water in the ne) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (        xt season. Mira, honored by his continued trust, returned even more generously.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
