BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      # The Spring of Threefold Return) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      In ancient times, when the world was young, there existed a sacred spring at the boundary ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        between two villages. The goddess of abundance had blessed it with a wondrous property: ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        any gift poured into its waters would triple before reaching the other side.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      The first villagers approached with caution. A farmer named Elena stood at the spring's ed) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        ge, clutching five copper coins. Fear whispered: "Keep what is yours." But trust urged h) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        er forward. She released three coins into the crystalline water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      As the coins sank, they shimmered and multiplied, becoming nine by the time they reached M) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        arcus on the opposite shore. He gazed at the unexpected bounty, understanding the spring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        's magic-and Elena's faith in him.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      The goddess watched, knowing this moment would define their future. Would Marcus honor the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (         gift, or betray the trust?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      Marcus carefully counted four coins and released them back across the spring. They did not) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (         multiply in return, yet both villagers stood richer than before-not just in copper, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (         in something more precious.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      From that day forward, the spring taught all who approached: generosity multiplies abundan) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (        ce, but only trust and reciprocity sustain it. Those who hoarded broke the sacred cycle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (         Those who gave and returned fairly prospered together, generation after generation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
