BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (      In ancient times, there lived a river spirit named Aquila who possessed five silver fish e) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (        ach dawn. Along the riverbank dwelt eight villages, and each day Aquila would visit one ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (        village, offering her bounty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      When Aquila gave her fish to a villager, the river's magic transformed them-each fish beca) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (        me three as it touched mortal hands. The villager could then choose: keep all the multip) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (        lied catch, or return some to Aquila's sacred pool.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (      The first villages were fearful and greedy. They clutched every fish tightly, returning no) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (        thing. Aquila still visited, still offered her five fish, but her spirit grew dim.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      Then came a village that understood the river's rhythm. When they received fifteen fish fr) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        om Aquila's gift of five, they returned seven to the sacred pool. Aquila's spirit bright) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (        ened, and when she visited again, her generosity flowed stronger.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      The wise villages learned: trust begets trust, and generosity returns like water to the se) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        a. When both spirit and mortal honored the cycle-one risking their gift, the other shari) Tj ET
