BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed from opposite mountains-the River of Silver and the Ri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 738.0 Td (        ver of Gold. Each was beautiful alone, but neither could reach the fertile valley below,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 728.0 Td (         for great stones blocked their paths.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 718.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 708.0 Td (      The River of Silver spoke first: "If I give you half my waters, will you help me reach the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 698.0 Td (         valley?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 688.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      The River of Gold was afraid. "What if you take all I offer and give nothing back?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (      But Silver replied, "See how the Sacred Spring works-whatever flows into it emerges three ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        times stronger. Let us trust in this magic.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      So Silver poured forth her waters. As they touched the Sacred Spring, they tripled in abun) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (        dance. Gold received this gift and was moved. In gratitude and wisdom, Gold returned eve) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (        n more than Silver had originally given.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      The waters merged and surged forward, washing away the stones. Together they reached the v) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (        alley, creating an oasis where all beings prospered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (      The Oracle proclaimed: "Blessed are those who trust first, for they create abundance. Bles) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (        sed are those who return generously, for they sustain it. But cursed are those who hoard) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (         or betray, for they shall forever remain alone behind their stones, watching others flo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        urish in the valley below.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      Here is the myth the other agent wrote in the previous round:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Endless Spring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      In ancient times, the goddess Themis discovered a sacred spring hidden in a valley between) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (         two villages. The spring possessed a miraculous property: any water poured into it woul) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        d triple before flowing downstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      Themis appeared to a villager named Doros and said, "You may pour water from your well int) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        o this spring. It will multiply and flow to your neighbor below. What they choose to ret) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        urn to you will determine whether this blessing continues.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      Doros, trusting in the goddess's wisdom, poured generously. The water tripled and flowed t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        o his neighbor, Alethia. Grateful and wise, Alethia returned a fair portion upstream to ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        Doros, keeping enough to nourish her own gardens.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      Seeing this harmony, Themis smiled and made the roles reverse with each moon. Sometimes Do) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        ros poured and received; sometimes Alethia. The cycle continued, and both villages flour) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        ished.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      But Themis warned: "This spring mirrors your hearts. Pour with trust, return with gratitud) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        e, and abundance flows eternal. But let suspicion or greed poison these waters, and the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (        spring will run dry for all.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      The villagers understood: prosperity flows not from hoarding, but from the endless cycle o) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        f giving and returning in balance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
