BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      **The Myth of the Twin Rivers**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed through a barren land-the River of Dawn and the River ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        of Dusk. Each possessed water, but neither could nurture the valley alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      The River of Dawn spoke first: "I shall send my waters forward, trusting they will return ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        enriched." And so it released its flow into the channels between them. As the waters tra) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        veled, they multiplied threefold, transformed by the valley's ancient magic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      The River of Dusk received this abundance and faced a choice. A voice whispered, "Keep all) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (         for yourself-you have received much." But Dusk remembered that dawn comes again, that r) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        ivers flow in cycles, not lines.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      "What flows to me came from trust," Dusk said. "I shall return enough that both of us flou) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        rish." And so Dusk sent back waters generously, keeping only what sustained its own cour) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (        se.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      Season after season, the rivers continued their exchange. Each learned the rhythm of givin) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (        g and receiving. When Dawn gave freely, Dusk returned fairly. The valley between them bl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (        oomed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      The elders say: prosperity flows not to those who hoard, but to those who understand that ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (        what moves through us must move onward. Trust multiplies what it touches, but only recip) Tj ET
