BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      In ancient times, the goddess Themis discovered a sacred spring hidden in a valley between) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (         two villages. The spring possessed a miraculous property: any water poured into it woul) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        d triple before flowing downstream.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      Themis appeared to a villager named Doros and said, "You may pour water from your well int) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        o this spring. It will multiply and flow to your neighbor below. What they choose to ret) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        urn to you will determine whether this blessing continues.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      Doros, trusting in the goddess's wisdom, poured generously. The water tripled and flowed t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (        o his neighbor, Alethia. Grateful and wise, Alethia returned a fair portion upstream to ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        Doros, keeping enough to nourish her own gardens.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      Seeing this harmony, Themis smiled and made the roles reverse with each moon. Sometimes Do) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        ros poured and received; sometimes Alethia. The cycle continued, and both villages flour) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        ished.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      But Themis warned: "This spring mirrors your hearts. Pour with trust, return with gratitud) Tj ET
