BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      In the beginning, two rivers flowed from opposite mountains-the River of Silver and the Ri) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        ver of Gold. Each was beautiful alone, but neither could reach the fertile valley below,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (         for great stones blocked their paths.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (      The River of Silver spoke first: "If I give you half my waters, will you help me reach the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (         valley?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      The River of Gold was afraid. "What if you take all I offer and give nothing back?") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      But Silver replied, "See how the Sacred Spring works-whatever flows into it emerges three ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (        times stronger. Let us trust in this magic.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
